        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16-a2">

                <pb facs="0347" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg337"/>

                <head>Appendix B to HD–100</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-25"><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 25,
                            1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: M. Foch.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: General Niessel, President of the Interallied Commissions
                    on Baltic Territories, Tilsitt.</p>
                <p>“In accord with the Conference:</p>
                <p>I approve all measures taken in order to put a stop to the Lithuanian attacks
                    against the Chavli-Tauroggen railway.</p>
                <p>Full authority is given to you by the Conference, to assure the evacuation of the
                    Baltic provinces by the Germans, and consequently, to take in Berlin the action
                    which you might deem proper.</p>
                <p>Any intervention of the Conference would only weaken your action, and would run
                    the risk of being too late.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
